Traefik answers on this Mac's ports 80 and 443, at localhost and at the Mac's
LAN address, with no root. An Ingress reaches it with a Host header:

  curl -H 'Host: your.host' http://localhost/
  curl -k -H 'Host: your.host' https://localhost/

or with a line in /etc/hosts for that name. HTTPS uses the Secret an Ingress
names under spec.tls, and Traefik's own certificate otherwise. Its
IngressClass, traefik, is the default, so an Ingress that names no class is
served here.

Only one ferry cluster on this Mac -- and one controller in it -- can have
port 80. With ingress-nginx enabled too, whichever came second says PortInUse
(kubectl -n traefik describe svc traefik) and is reached on its node port, and
an Ingress that names no class goes to whichever was enabled last.
